.TH KWAAINET 1 "2026-09-04" "KwaaiNet" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
kwaainet \- KwaaiNet node CLI for decentralized inference and training
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B kwaainet
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.I COMMAND
.RI [ ARGS ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B kwaainet
runs and controls a node on KwaaiNet, a libp2p peer-to-peer network for
sovereign AI: decentralized model inference, distributed transformer block
sharding, and private vector storage.
.PP
A node joins the network through bootstrap peers, announces the model blocks it
can serve, and discovers other nodes over a distributed hash table. Nodes behind
NAT connect via hole punching or relay circuits, so no port forwarding is
required in the common case.
.PP
The node process is backed by
.BR p2pd (1),
a libp2p daemon shipped alongside this binary. Configuration and state, including
the node identity key, live under
.IR ~/.kwaainet .
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B start
Start the KwaaiNet node.
.TP
.B stop
Stop the KwaaiNet daemon.
.TP
.B restart
Restart the KwaaiNet daemon.
.TP
.B run\-node
Run the node in the foreground. This is the entry point used by the systemd
service unit; prefer
.B start
interactively.
.TP
.B status
Show daemon status.
.TP
.B logs
Show daemon logs.
.TP
.B config
View or modify configuration.
.TP
.B node\-health
Live health check: p2pd, Ollama, and relay circuit status.
.TP
.B service
Manage the auto\-start service.
.TP
.B p2p
Inspect live p2p state, such as identity and connected peers.
.TP
.B shard
Distributed transformer block sharding: serve a range of blocks, coordinate
inference across peers, or inspect block coverage on the network.
.TP
.B serve
Serve an OpenAI\-compatible API backed by the local model.
.TP
.B storage
Manage the local storage fabric.
.TP
.B vpk
Manage VPK (Virtual Private Knowledge) vector database integration.
.TP
.B update
Check or install updates. Disabled in packaged installs; see
.B NOTES
below.
.PP
This is not the full command set. Run
.B kwaainet \-\-help
for the complete list, and
.BI "kwaainet " COMMAND " \-\-help"
for the options of any one command.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-h ", " \-\-help
Print help.
.TP
.B \-V ", " \-\-version
Print version.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B KWAAINET_NO_AUTO_UPDATE
When set to
.BR 1 ,
the node does not check for or install updates. Set by default in
.IR /etc/default/kwaainet .
.TP
.B RUST_LOG
Log filter, e.g.
.BR kwaainet=debug .
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.kwaainet/config.yaml
Node configuration.
.TP
.I ~/.kwaainet/identity.key
Node identity key. Never removed by package upgrade or removal.
.TP
.I ~/.kwaainet/logs/kwaainet.log
Node log.
.TP
.I /etc/default/kwaainet
Environment for the packaged systemd user unit.
.TP
.I /usr/lib/systemd/user/kwaainet.service
Packaged systemd user unit. Not enabled on install.
.SH NOTES
This package installs KwaaiNet from a distribution package. Self\-update is
disabled, because it would replace files the package manager owns. Upgrade with
.B apt
instead. See
.I /usr/share/doc/kwaainet/README.Debian
for details.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR systemctl (1)
.PP
Project home:
.UR https://kwaai.ai
.UE
